# Copy to apps/mobile/.env and fill values from the shared Supabase project
# (same project as sibling Edubite / web — map NEXT_PUBLIC_* → EXPO_PUBLIC_*).
#
# NEVER put SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, Google Client Secret, or DB passwords here.
# Mobile may only use: project URL + anon/publishable key + public Google Web Client ID.
#
# Anonymous sign-ins are NOT used. App requires Google login at startup.
# Native Google Sign-In requires a development build (NOT Expo Go).
#
# Local preview only (__DEV__). Restart Expo after changing.
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SKIP_AUTH=1  → skip LoginGate (Expo Go scan / UI tour)
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SKIP_AUTH=0  → Google login required
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SKIP_AUTH=0

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://bytsiknhtcnlxwzgqkrd.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Google Cloud → Credentials → OAuth 2.0 Client IDs → Web application
# (Client ID ≠ ID token. ID token comes from GoogleSignin.signIn().)
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=167530443868-kniil90rorooo9i3vu80sqmtlo3sqqi2.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Optional deep-link override (native builds default to edubite://auth/callback).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URL=edubite://auth/callback

# --- Dashboard checklist (Google native ID-token → Supabase) ---
# 1) Google Cloud → confirm EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID Application type = Web application.
#    Keep Web Authorized redirect URI for Edublast web:
#      https://bytsiknhtcnlxwzgqkrd.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback
# 2) Create a separate Android OAuth client:
#      Package name: com.edubite.app
#      SHA-1: from `eas credentials` / local debug keystore / upload key
# 3) Supabase → Authentication → Providers → Google:
#    - Authorized Client IDs (comma-separated):
#        <WEB_CLIENT_ID>,<ANDROID_CLIENT_ID>
#    - Client secret: Web client secret only
#    - Enable "Skip nonce check" (required for current RN Google Sign-In Original API)
# 4) Build + install Android dev client (not Expo Go):
#      cd apps/mobile && npx eas build --profile development --platform android
#      # or: npx expo run:android
# 5) Start Metro and open the custom Edubite app:
#      npm run start --workspace=mobile
